WEBVTT

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:16.000
Episode 43 · 10 March 2026
North and south vents fountain together, feeding lava channels across the crater floor.

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:31.000
Episode 44 · 9 April
Southerly winds carry the plume north. Tephra falls on the park, Highway 11 and nearby communities.

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:40.500
Episode 45 · 23 April, 1:34 to 10:01 a.m.
Only the north vent erupts. Its fountains reach about 870 ft (265 m).

00:00:40.500 --> 00:00:47.500
Slowed four times: filmed at 120 frames a second.

00:00:50.500 --> 00:00:55.500
Episode 46 · 5 May, from 8:17 a.m.
Fountains up to 650 ft (200 m).

00:00:55.500 --> 00:01:00.500
Slowed four times.

00:01:04.500 --> 00:01:13.500
Episode 48 · 1 June
The 48th episode: the most fountaining episodes of any one Kīlauea eruption.

00:01:13.500 --> 00:01:22.500
Episode 55 · 17 October, dawn
The plume rises to about 25,000 ft (7,600 m) above sea level.

00:01:22.500 --> 00:01:37.300
Episode 56 · 5 November
Six hours of fountaining, up to 660 ft (200 m), seen by the V1 webcam on the crater rim.
